This license covers the software, database scripts, data and documentation in
this repository (the "Materials"). It is not an open-source license.

1. Who may use the Materials

   You may use the Materials only if you are a registered or invited
   participant in, or an instructor of, an Athanor workshop run by
   CODE Éxitos (a "Session").

2. What you may do

   From the time you are invited to a Session until that Session ends, you
   may:

   a. view, download and clone the Materials, and copy them into one private
      repository of your own (for example with GitHub's "Use this template");
   b. build, run, analyze and change them on your own device or in a cloud
      development environment you control, such as GitHub Codespaces; and
   c. process them with AI coding assistants and analysis tools to prepare
      for and complete the Session's exercises, provided those tools are not
      configured to use your inputs to train or improve AI models.

3. What you may not do

   You may not:

   a. publish, distribute, sublicense, sell or otherwise share the Materials or
      any changed version of them, including by pushing them to any public or
      shared repository, package registry or file-sharing service;
   b. keep a public fork of this repository;
   c. use the Materials, or any part of them, in any product, service,
      production system or commercial activity;
   d. use the Materials to create or deliver training, courses or workshops;
   e. use the Materials to train, fine-tune or evaluate AI or machine-learning
      models.

4. After the Session

   When the Session ends, you must delete every copy of the Materials and of
   any changed version of them, including any repository copy and Codespace
   you created for the Session. You may keep your own notes about what you
   learned, as long as they do not reproduce substantial parts of the
   Materials.

5. Fictional content

   All companies, people, aircraft and data in the Materials are fictional.
   Any resemblance to real organizations, people or systems is coincidental.

6. Third-party components

   Some files in this repository are third-party components (the jQuery,
   jQuery UI, Bootstrap, Modernizr and Respond.js script, style and font
   files). They are licensed under their own terms, which are included with
   them, and this license does not apply to them.

7. Ending this license

   Your permission under this license ends automatically if you break any of
   its terms. When it ends, you must stop using the Materials and delete all
   copies.

8. No warranty and no liability

   The Materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express
   or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose and non-infringement. To the fullest extent permitted by
   law, CODE Éxitos is not liable for any claim, damage or other liability
   arising from the Materials or your use of them.

